---
import PublicResourcePage from '../../components/content/PublicResourcePage.astro';
const sections = [
  {
    heading: 'Calculation engines',
    paragraphs: [
      'Each calculator uses a small, focused calculation engine that validates the information you enter and returns structured numeric results.',
      "The page then formats those results for the selected country and language. It does not quietly substitute another country's rules when a specific jurisdiction is selected.",
    ],
  },
  {
    heading: 'Tax-year data',
    paragraphs: [
      'Each page identifies the tax year supported by its data when a tax year applies.',
      'The current release focuses on 2026 data for pages that display a 2026 tax year. When a new tax year is published, the relevant data and calculator assumptions should be reviewed again.',
    ],
  },
  {
    heading: 'Rounding and display',
    paragraphs: [
      "The calculation engine keeps numeric precision during the calculation and formats the final amounts for display using the selected locale's currency and number conventions.",
      "Pay-period amounts can differ slightly from an employer's final paycheck because real payroll systems may use different rounding and payment schedules.",
    ],
  },
  {
    heading: 'Assumptions and country rules',
    paragraphs: [
      'Each calculator supports a defined set of inputs. Depending on the tool, that can include standard deductions, progressive tax brackets, social insurance, state rules, proportional estimates, or employment-related limits.',
      'Benefits, local taxes, collective agreements, unusual legal exceptions, and personal circumstances may fall outside the supported model.',
    ],
  },
  {
    heading: 'Estimates versus official payroll',
    paragraphs: [
      'A PayRenTax result is an estimate.',
      'It is not an official payslip, tax assessment, legal calculation, or employer payroll output. Always read the included and excluded items on the relevant calculator page before relying on the result.',
    ],
  },
  {
    heading: 'Testing and updates',
    paragraphs: [
      'The project uses tests for calculation arithmetic, input validation, representative scenarios, route registration, and important SEO behavior.',
      'When an official threshold or rule changes, the related data module, tests, documentation, and page review information should be updated together.',
    ],
  },
];
---

<PublicResourcePage
  title="How PayRenTax Calculators Work"
  description="Learn how PayRenTax calculation engines handle inputs, tax-year data, rounding, country rules, assumptions, and testing."
  canonical="/how-calculators-work/"
  sections={sections}
  eyebrow="Methodology"
/>
